@* Upstream's own: one small outline toggle with an icon and a word. The bookmark fills when the
   toggle is pressed — upstream writes that as group-aria-pressed/toggle, and here the pressed
   state is a real checked checkbox inside the label, so it is group-has-[:checked]/toggle. Same
   idea: the child styles itself from the state of the control it is inside. *@
<Toggle Size="sm" Variant="outline" Name="bookmark" aria-label="Toggle bookmark">
    <Icon Name="bookmark" Class="group-has-[:checked]/toggle:fill-foreground" />
    Bookmark
</Toggle>
